From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MIRAGE <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:52:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] MIRAGE: ordinary commands answer as a real Debian 12 host
 does

Found by holding the emulator against a real host with the fingerprint
suite. A new module, loaded last, replaces ls, id, wc, who, w and env and
adds sort, stat, type and command -v, each written from a record of what
GNU coreutils 9.1, procps 4 and bash 5.2 print:

- ls: one name to a line without a terminal, columns filled downwards with
  tab padding on one, a header for each of several directories, a total and
  real link counts and dates in the long format, exit status 2;
- the shell expands *, ? and [...] in unquoted words, and a leading ~;
- the session's environment is what sshd and PAM set (SSH_CONNECTION,
  SSH_CLIENT, MOTD_SHOWN; no TMOUT; UID is not exported; SHLVL 0 for an
  exec request);
- who and w show a login only for a session with a terminal.

The gate's tier now says 'none' for a program that exists in the filesystem
and that nothing emulates (the stand-in could only print 'cannot execute
binary file'), and for options a command declines.
